{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"text":" so they don’t block UI. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","text":"4. Persistence is invisible","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" records every change in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","level":2,"text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding(get:set:)"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","level":2,"text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","level":2,"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","level":2,"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","level":2,"text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Protocol","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"type":"text","text":" (any JSON host)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Struct of closures","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configure or mock it: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SyncPreflightService"},{"type":"text","text":". Closures make the built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".live"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".mock"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaced."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Anti-patterns","level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@StateObject"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Design Principles"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"]},{"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"title":"Explanation"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"title":"PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"title":"binding(_:sending:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","text":"KeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]}},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"title":"Send","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"title":"ChangeSet","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"title":"SwiduxPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"title":"StateWriter","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"title":"Build Your First Swidux App","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"}}}